// Rule: [T1505.003][T1059] Hermes Hades - Webserver to Hadoop Service
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1505.003, T1059
// Classification: Validation query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceNetworkEvents
// Purpose: Validating source-observed connections from compromised web infrastructure to HiveServer2 and WebHDFS.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceNetworkEvents for webserver to hadoop service using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: An inventoried web server initiated traﬃc to an inventoried Hadoop node on a source- observed service port. What it does not prove Web shell, successful authentication, UDF execution, data access, exfiltration or attribution.
// A match does not prove: a web shell, successful Hive authentication, UDF creation, command execution, data access, or Hermes/Hades attribution.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// Web server to Hadoop service connectivity validation
// Classification: Validation query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting
// Required telemetry: DeviceNetworkEvents from every web server in scope
//
// Hunt.io directly documented tooling that used a compromised web server as
// the launch point for HiveServer2 and WebHDFS access on TCP 10000 and 50070.
// Replace both inventories before execution. They are required controls, not
// optional allowlists.
let WebServerDevices = dynamic(["<WEB_SERVER_FQDN>"]);
let HadoopNodeIPs = dynamic(["<HADOOP_NODE_IP>"]);
DeviceNetworkEvents
| where DeviceName in~ (WebServerDevices)
| where RemoteIP in (HadoopNodeIPs)
| where RemotePort in (10000, 50070)
| project
    Timestamp,
    DeviceId,
    DeviceName,
    LocalIP,
    RemoteIP,
    RemotePort,
    RemoteUrl,
    Protocol,
    ActionType,
    InitiatingProcessFileName,
    InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
    InitiatingProcessAccountName,
    InitiatingProcessSHA1,
    ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc

// Interpretation:
// A result proves only that an inventoried web server initiated network
// activity toward an inventoried Hadoop node on a source-observed service port.
// It does not prove a web shell, successful Hive authentication, UDF creation,
// command execution, data access, or Hermes/Hades attribution.
//
// Validate:
// 1. Confirm complete web-server and Hadoop-node inventories.
// 2. Identify legitimate applications, service accounts, processes and flows.
// 3. Confirm ActionType semantics and process/command-line population.
// 4. Corroborate unexplained matches with web, HiveServer2, HDFS and EDR logs.
